          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Traditional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+quantization"} geometric quantization
            applies to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+manifolds"} symplectic manifolds
            but not to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson+manifolds"} Poisson manifolds
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+Lie+n-algebroid"} symplectic Lie n-algebroid
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson+Lie+algebroid"} Poisson Lie algebroid
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+symplectic+geometry"} higher symplectic geometry
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+integration"} Lie integration
            is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+groupoid"} symplectic groupoid
          %p
            There is an generalization of the machinery of geometric quantization to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+groupoids"} symplectic groupoids
            which hence provides a geometric quantization of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson+manifolds"} Poisson manifolds
          %h2#definition Definition
          %h3#GeometricPrequantization Geometric prequantization of a symplectic groupoid
          %p
            Formulated in the language of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+differential+geometry"} higher differential geometry
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prequantization"} prequantization
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+groupoid"} symplectic groupoid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi SG
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi π
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi exp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝔓
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi π
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SG(X,\pi) = \exp(\mathfrak{P}(X,\pi))
            (see
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#EH"} Hawkins, section 4.2
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+infinity-groupoids"} smooth 2-groupoids
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi SG
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi π
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⟶
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mn 2
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi conn
                        %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  SG(X,\pi) \longrightarrow \mathbf{B}^2 U(1)_{conn^1}
          %p
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+infinity-stack"} moduli 2-stack
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+n-bundle+with+connection"} circle 2-bundles with 1-form connection
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson+manifold"} Poisson manifold
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↙
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↘
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo *
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ⇙
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi SG
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi X
                          %mo ,
                          %mi π
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↘
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mo ↙
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mover
                                %mi χ
                                %mo ^
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi B
                            %mn 2
                          %mi U
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 1
                          %msub
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mrow
                              %msup
                                %mi conn
                                %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \&amp;&amp; X
                  \\\
                  \&amp; \swarrow &amp;&amp; \searrow
                  \\\
                  \\ast &amp;&amp; \swArrow &amp;&amp; SG(X,\pi)
                  \\\
                  \&amp; \searrow &amp;&amp; \swarrow_{\mathrlap{\widehat{\chi}}}
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; \mathbf{B}^2 U(1)_{conn^1}
                  }
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#hgp"}> hgp 13
            ,
            %a{:href => "#Bongers13"} Bongers 13
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Nuiten13"} Nuiten 13
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi χ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-Lie+algebra+cohomology"} Lie algebroid cohomology
            (hence in
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson+cohomology"} Poisson cohomology
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi π
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi CE
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝔓
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi π
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi \in CE^\bullet(\mathfrak{P}(X,\pi))
          %p
            By (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Higher+Chern-Weil+Derivation+of+AKSZ+Sigma-Models"}> FRS 11
            , based on
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Cech+Cocycles+for+Differential+characteristic+Classes"} FSS 10
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi π
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi 𝔓
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi π
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\pi \;\colon\; \mathfrak{P}(X,\pi) \longrightarrow \mathbb{R}[2]
          %p
            directly
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+integration"} Lie integrates
            to a morphism of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+infinity-groupoids"} smooth 2-groupoids
            of the form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi exp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi π
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi conn
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi SG
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi π
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi conn
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi τ
                    %mn 1
                  %mi exp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝔓
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi π
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi conn
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi Γ
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi conn
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\exp(\pi)_{conn}
                  \\;\colon\;
                  SG(X,\pi)_{conn} = \tau_1 \exp(\mathfrak{P}(X,\pi))_{conn}
                  \\longrightarrow
                  \\mathbf{B}(\mathbb{R}/\Gamma)_{conn}
                  \\,,
          %p
            which is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocycle"} cocycle
            in degree-3
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+differential+cohomology"} ordinary differential cohomology
            on the differential refinement
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi SG
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi π
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi conn
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SG(X,\pi)_{conn}
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+groupoid"} symplectic groupoid
            by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-Lie+algebroid-valued+differential+form"} Lie algebroid valued differential forms
            (the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stack"} moduli stack
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2d+Chern-Simons+theory"} 2d Chern-Simons theory
            induced by the cocycle), with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficients"} coefficients
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient"} quotient
            group
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi Γ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}/\Gamma
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma \hookrightarrow \mathbb{R}
            is the group of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/periods"} periods
            of
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %mi T
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi 𝔓
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi π
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi π
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo )
                  %mo ∈
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi cl
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\left(
                  T S^2 \longrightarrow \mathfrak{P}(X,\pi) \stackrel{\pi}{\longrightarrow} \mathbb{R}[2]
                  \\right)
                  \\in \Omega^2_{cl}(S^2)
                  \\,.
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo =
                  %mi ℤ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma = \mathbb{Z}
            this hence yields
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi SG
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi π
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi τ
                    %mn 1
                  %mi exp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝔓
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi π
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi conn
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi conn
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  SG(X,\pi) = \tau_1 \exp(\mathfrak{P}(X,\pi))_{conn}
                  \\longrightarrow
                  \\mathbf{B}U(1)_{conn}
                  \\,.
          %p
            This integrality condition is the one that appears in the traditional literature as (
            %a{:href => "#BonechiCattaneoZabzine05"}> Bonechi-Cattaneo-Zabzine 05, (1.7)-(1.11)
            ) based on (
            %a{:href => "#CrainicZhu04"}> Crainic-Zhu 04, theorem 3
            ).
          %p
            Forgetting the differential refinement and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+2-connection"} principal 2-connection
            structure we get an underlying
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+2-group"} circle 2-group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+2-bundle"} principal 2-bundle
            on the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+groupoid"} symplectic groupoid
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi exp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi π
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi SH
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi π
