            %a{:href => "#GBV"}> GBV 94
            ,
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#EH"} EH 06, example 6.2
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+manifold"}> symplectic manifold
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+quantization"} geometric quantization
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C-star+algebraic+deformation+quantization"} C-star algebraic deformation quantization
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson+Lie+algebroid"} Poisson Lie algebroid
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mo ↦
                        %mrow
                          %mi exp
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \stackrel{\exp(-)}{\mapsto}
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+groupoid"} symplectic groupoid
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mo ↦
                        %mrow
                          %mi central
                          %mi extension
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \stackrel{central extension}{\mapsto}
                %strong geometric quantization of symplectic groupoids
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+Lie+n-algebroid"} symplectic Lie n-algebroid
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mo ↦
                        %mrow
                          %mi exp
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \stackrel{\exp(-)}{\mapsto}
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} symplectic ∞-groupoid
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mo ↦
                        %mrow
                          %mi central
                          %mi extension
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \stackrel{central extension}{\mapsto}
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+quantization+of+symplectic+%E2%88%9E-groupoids"} geometric quantization of symplectic ∞-groupoids
          %h2#references References
          %p Symplectic groupoids were introduced as intended tools for the quantization of Poisson manifolds in
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alan+Weinstein"}> Alan Weinstein
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Symplectic groupoids and Poisson manifolds
                %em Symplectic groupoids, geometric quantization, and irrational rotation algebras
                in
              %p
                %em Symplectic geometry, groupoids, and integrable systems
                (Berkeley, CA, 1989), 281–290, Springer, New York, (1991) MR1104934;
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Tangential deformation quantization and polarized symplectic groupoids
                %em Deformation theory and symplectic geometry
                (Ascona, 1996), 301–314, Kluwer (1997)
                %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=1480730"} MR1480730
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alan+Weinstein"}> Alan Weinstein
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ping+Xu"} Ping Xu
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Extensions of symplectic groupoids and quantization
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.digizeitschriften.de/dms/img/?PPN=GDZPPN00220858X"} pdf
            %li
              %p S. Zakrzewski, Quantum and classical pseudogroups I, II, Commun. Math. Phys. 134 (1990)
          %p
            Their
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prequantization"} prequantization
            is developed in
          %ul#LGX
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Camille+Laurent-Gengoux"}> Camille Laurent-Gengoux
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ping+Xu"} Ping Xu
              %em Quantization of pre-quasi-symplectic groupoids and their Hamiltonian spaces
              in
              %em The Breadth of Symplectic and Poisson Geometry
              Progress in Mathematics, 2005, Volume 232, 423-454 (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0311154"}> arXiv:math/0311154
              )
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marius+Crainic"}> Marius Crainic
                ,
                %em Prequantization and Lie brackets
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0403269"}> arXiv:0403269
                )
            %li#CrainicZhu04
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marius+Crainic"}> Marius Crainic
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chenchang+Zhu"} Chenchang Zhu
                %em Integrability of Jacobi structures
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0403268"}> arXiv:math/0403268
                )
            %li#BonechiCattaneoZabzine05
              %p
                Francesco Bonechi,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alberto+Cattaneo"} Alberto Cattaneo
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Maxim+Zabzine"} Maxim Zabzine
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Geometric quantization and non-perturbative Poisson sigma model
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0507223"} arXiv:math/0507223
          %p
            A notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/polarization"} polarization
            and of actual
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+quantization"} geometric quantization
            of symplectic groupoids, yielding a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+deformation+quantization"} strict deformation quantization
            of the underlying Poisson manifold, originates in
          %ul
            %li#Weinstein91
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alan+Weinstein"}> Alan Weinstein
              ,
              %em Noncommutative geometry and geometric quantization
              in P. Donato et al. (eds.)
              = succeed "," do
                %em Symplectic geometry and Mathematical physics
          %p
            and is further developed, via
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid+convolution+algebra"} groupoid convolution algebra
          %ul
            %li#EH
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eli+Hawkins"}> Eli Hawkins
              \:
              = succeed "," do
                %em A groupoid approach to quantization
              %strong 6
              1 (2008) 61-125 [
              %a{:href => "https://projecteuclid.org/journals/journal-of-symplectic-geometry/volume-6/issue-1/A-groupoid-approach-to-quantization/jsg/1215032733.full"}> jsg:1215032733
              ,
              = succeed "]" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math.SG/0612363"} arXiv:math.SG/0612363
          %p
            The case over Poisson vector spaces leading to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Moyal+quantization"} Moyal quantization
            was proven earlier in
          %ul
            %li#GBV
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jos%C3%A9+Gracia-Bondia"}> José Gracia-Bondia
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Joseph+Varilly"} Joseph Varilly
              = succeed "," do
                %em From geometric quantization to Moyal quantization
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9406170"} arXiv:hep-th/9406170
          %p and had been claimed without proof in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alan+Weinstein"}> Alan Weinstein
              , in P. Donato et al. (eds.)
              %em Symplectic Geometry and Mathematical Physics, (Birkhäuser, Basel, 1991); p. 446.
          %p
            The interpretation of symplectic groupoids in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+geometry"} higher geometry
            is made fairly explicit in (
            %a{:href => "#LGX"}> LGX
            ) above. This is further expanded on in
          %ul
            %li#hgp13
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Domenico+Fiorenza"}> Domenico Fiorenza
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chris+Rogers"} Chris Rogers
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Higher+geometric+prequantum+theory"} Higher geometric prequantum theory
                2013
            %li#Bongers13
              %p
                Stefan Bongers, section 4 of
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/master+thesis+Bongers"} Geometric quantization of symplectic and Poisson manifolds
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/motivic+quantization"} cohomological quantization
            of symplectic groupoids in this sense, making the construction in (
            %a{:href => "#Weinstein91"}> Weinstein 91
            ,
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#EH"} Hawkins 08
          %ul
            %li#Nuiten13
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Joost+Nuiten"}> Joost Nuiten
              , section 5.2.2 of
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/master+thesis+Nuiten"} Cohomological quantization of local boundary prequantum field theory
        .revisedby
